    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2SRHUWz5F2if6VxPkp4VonS)_\n\n## What\n\n- `gh-pr-pdf` now starts every PR on a new page in the PDF.\n- It no longer fails to build the PDF on PR text where inline code is followed by `.name`.\n\n## Cause\n\n- The committed `.typ` (366 PRs, pandoc and Typst 0.15) compiles with every PR, so the org files and that snapshot are fine.\n- A fresh re-render of the same backup with pandoc 3.9 failed in `typst compile` with `raw does not have field \"el\"`.\n  - pandoc writes inline code as `#raw(\"...\")`.\n  - Typst reads `#raw(\"...\").el` as field access, not as text.\n  - PRs #64, #93, #176 and #271 trigger it: their source has nested backticks, so pandoc leaves `.el` or `.gitignore` right after the span.\n- The failed compile left the previous PDF in place, so the PDF looked current but lacked the newer PRs, and compiling again fails the same way.\n- I could not see Sia's PDF, so this is the cause I reproduced, not a proven match for their exact output.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `harden_typst` puts a zero-width space after `#raw(...)` when `.letter` follows. Only `#raw` calls are touched (table code such as `(auto, auto).at(col)` needs its dot).\n- The preamble gets `#show heading.where(level: 1)` with a weak `pagebreak`: one PR (or discussion) per page.\n- The old PDF is deleted before `typst compile`, so a failure cannot leave a stale one.\n- `README.org` documents the three points as bullets.\n\n## Checked\n\n- Re-rendered all 366 PRs from the committed backup with pandoc 3.9 and Typst 0.15: PDF builds, 507 pages (was 294), all 366 PR headings present, each starting its own page.\n\n## Not checked\n\n- Not run on Sia's Mac, so their pandoc and Typst versions were not tried.\n- With pandoc 3.1.3 the Typst build fails with `expected colon`, with or without this change. This is a separate pandoc-version problem, not touched here.\n- No `CHANGELOG.org` change, per the rules.\n- The branch name has no PR-number prefix (the branch is fixed by the environment).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi8mA91YKqdvxXiwQZF)_",
